38	- Identifying a relative linear system with Proj(pi_*L) across loci where h^0(L) jumps, or treating the balanced reduced-support relative linear system as a closed pure-codimension-four subvariety of M_{6,6}. [reason: Proj(pi_*L) has the correct fibres only over the open locus of constant h^0; and the reduced-support locus is an open piece of the evaluation-failure locus, so a Gysin/localization argument for the pair (M_{6,6}, Z) needs a closed (stratified) embedding obtained after h^0 and splitting-type stratification.]
