- By Serre duality h^1(L) = h^0(omega_C tensor L^{-1}) = h^0(omega_C^{tensor 2} tensor W_5^vee), and deg(omega_C^{tensor 2} tensor W_5^vee) = 2(2g-2) - (4g+12-4f) at g=6, f=5 equals 20-16 = 4; hence h^0(L) = 1 + h^0(M) with M := omega_C^{tensor 2} tensor W_5^vee a degree-4 line bundle. [evidence: mechanical; omega_C tensor L^{-1} = omega_C tensor omega_C tensor W_5^vee; degree 2*10 - 16 = 4. Combined with chi(L)=1 this gives h^0(L)=1+h^1(L)=1+h^0(M). Uses no identification of W_5 with omega_C^{tensor 2}(-D).]
- At (g,n)=(6,6) the Poincare-duality dictionary specializes correctly to the stated target data: d = 3*6-3+6 = 21 and 2d-16 = 26, matching dimension 21, Poincare twist 21, and ordinary cohomological degree 26. [evidence: mechanical; 3g-3+n = 18-3+6 = 21; 2*21-16 = 26. These agree with the target fields dimension=21, poincare_twist=21, ordinary_cohomology_degree=26, open_bm_degree=16.]
- For the Casnati–Ekedahl bundle W_f on a genus-g degree-four cover, deg(W_f|_C)=4g+12-4f. [evidence: source; The quoted lemma gives the degree formula deg(W_{f_i}|_C)=4g+12-4f_i.]
- Irreducible components of I|_{H_3} correspond bijectively to irreducible components of H_3, so I|_{H_3} is irreducible if and only if H_3 is irreducible. [evidence: source; Section 3.1 applies Zariski-local triviality with irreducible fibre P^2, which preserves and reflects irreducible components.]
- The CE obstruction decomposes as H^0(C, omega_C tensor W|_C^vee(Gamma))=oplus_i H^0(C, omega_C tensor W_{f_i}|_C^vee(Gamma)), and the obstruction line bundle for summand f has degree 4f+n-2g-14. [evidence: source; SRC-0004 Lemma 10.6: deg(omega tensor W_f^vee(Gamma))=2g-2-(4g+12-4f)+n=4f+n-2g-14.]
- For a degree-four cover gamma: C -> P^1 with Casnati-Ekedahl bundles W_{f_i} = O_{P(E^vee)}(2) tensor gamma^*O(-f_i), one has deg(O_{P(E^vee)}(2)|_C) = 2(2g-2+4*2) and deg(W_f|_C) = 4g+12-4f; for g=6 this gives deg(O_{P(E^vee)}(2)|_C) = 36, deg W_5 = 16 and deg W_4 = 20. [evidence: source; Packet C66-001-v4, Primary locator excerpt SRC-0004 Lemma 10.6 (degree/Serre-duality calculation), together with the packet bullet 'Degree calculation: deg(W_f|_C)=4g+12-4f'.]
- For the Casnati–Ekedahl line bundles on a smooth genus-6 curve, deg(W_f|_C)=4g+12-4f, so deg(W_5)=16 and deg(W_5⊗ω_C^{-1})=6. [evidence: source; Packet primary locator SRC-0004 Lemma 10.6 and canonical geometric bottleneck degree calculation.]
- With W_f := (O_{P(E^vee)}(2) tensor gamma^*O_{P^1}(-f))|_C, one has deg(W_f)=4g+12-4f; the negative sign is essential. [evidence: source; SRC-0004, Lemma 10.6, gives deg(W_f|_C)=2(2g-2+8)-4f=4g+12-4f using gamma^*O(-f).]
- For the Casnati–Ekedahl summands W_{f_i}=O_{P(E^vee)}(2)⊗γ^*O(−f_i) restricted to C, deg(W_{f_i}|_C)=2(2g−2+4·2)−4f_i=4g+12−4f_i. [evidence: source; SRC-0004 Lemma 10.6 packet excerpt: deg W_fi|C = 2(2g−2+4·2)−4fi = 4g+12−4fi.]
