- `FND-0069` [corroborated; {'attempt_id': 'ATT-0026', 'campaign_id': 'C66-001', 'subproblem_id': 'C66-GEO-Z'}]: The Petri-general fibre calculation proves a smooth 17-dimensional dominant component, but global claims about codim Z require excluding larger components over special curve loci and distinguishing component existence from purity.
- `FND-0071` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: A low-degree diagonal statement that, at 2r=2g+n-2, only the kernel of restriction H^{2r}(\overline{M}_{g,n})→H^{2r}(D) is Tate does not by itself make the whole group H^{2r}(\overline{M}_{g,n}) Tate; boundary-supported classes and the full stratified contribution must still be controlled.
- `FND-0072` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: No complete unconditional proof that H^{16}(\overline{M}_{6,6};Q) is a direct sum of Q(-8) is supplied by ATT-0027; graph-complex/arc-contraction slogans without Aut-invariants, Gysin shifts, differentials, and higher-genus primitives do not discharge this.
- `FND-0073` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: On any smooth genus-6 geometric fibre of the balanced tetragonal CE family, h^0(L) = 1 + h^0(M) where M := ω_C^2⊗W_5^∨ has deg M = 2(2g-2) - (4g+12-4f)|_{g=6,f=5} = 20 - 16 = 4. This follows from χ(L)=1 plus Serre duality h^1(L) = h^0(ω_C⊗L^{-1}) = h^0(ω_C^2⊗W_5^∨), and uses no part of the undischarged GAP-Z-W5D identification W_5 ≅ ω_C^2(-D). Consequently the C66-GEO-H0 stratification of the relative degree-six linear system by h^0(L) is exactly the stratification of a relative degree-4 line bundle by h^0, i.e. a g^1_4-type Brill-Noether question in degree 4 rather than degree 6, with h^0(L)=3 (fibrewise |L| ≅ P^2) precisely where h^0(M)=2.
- `FND-0074` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: Substituting g=6 into the SRC-0004 obstruction degree 4f+n-2g-14 gives n-10 for f=4 and n-6 for f=5. Hence for all n ≤ 9 the f=4 summand vanishes identically and the whole CE obstruction is carried by the f=5 summand; for n ≤ 5 the f=5 summand also has negative degree so the failure locus is empty; at n=6 the f=5 obstruction has degree exactly 0, which is the unique value making the failure condition a single Abel-Jacobi condition O_C(Γ) ≅ L rather than a positive-degree Brill-Noether condition (n ≥ 7). The identification proved for (6,6) is therefore structurally specific to the borderline degree and does not transport to neighbouring n by the same argument.
- `FND-0075` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: The finite étale S_6-torsor Conf_6 → (reduced-support open) holds on the stack of pairwise-distinct sections and fails on coarse moduli at curves whose automorphisms permute the marked points. Downstream nodes that descend a cohomology or weight computation from the ordered model to the unordered one must therefore work with stack (orbifold) cohomology; with Q-coefficients S_6-invariants and S_6-coinvariants agree, so the descent is harmless rationally, but the same descent is not available integrally and is not available on the coarse space. Any integral-coefficient or coarse-space version of a C66-TATE-* argument built on this model needs an independent justification.
