- `FND-0092` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: The standard ordered 0-filling system of 2g arcs a1,b1,...,ag,bg (standard 4g-gon side identification) represents the zero class in the Steinberg module St of Mod_{g,1}/Mod_g. Broaddus cyclicity uses a different nontrivial generator phi0. Any top-degree vanishing argument that takes the standard filling-system class as a cyclic generator fixed by handle half-turns is vacuous and does not compute (St tensor V)_G.
- `FND-0093` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: For (g,n)=(6,6), the five-stage forgetful Leray-plus-residue argument with r=6-j correctly produces a surjection Gr^W_26 H^{21}(M_{6,1};H^{tensor 5}) onto Gr^W_26 H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q) (weight floor 27 kills residue quotients on Gr^W_26; FND-0037 connecting maps affect kernels only). This reduces exact-target vanishing to odd-tensor vcd vanishing on M_{6,1} and does not by itself prove the RED-0001 corner.
- `FND-0096` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'generality': 'all g >= 1, n >= 1'}]: The universal determinantal computation underlying C66-GEO-Z is not specific to (g,n) = (6,6). For any g >= 1 and any n >= 1, with Gamma a relative Cartier divisor finite etale of degree n over the base and L_univ = omega_{C_P/P}(Gamma_P) tensor Poin^{-1} on C x_S Pic^0(C/S), one has Fit_0(coker(p_*L_univ -> p_*(L_univ|_{Gamma_P}))) = I_e. Reason: deg L_univ = 2g-2+n > 2g-2 gives R^1p_* = 0 and h^0 = g+n-1; at e the kernel is H^0(omega) of dimension g and the cokernel is H^1(omega) of dimension 1 for EVERY n >= 1, so Hom(ker,coker) has dimension g = dim T_e Pic^0, and the intrinsic derivative is the Serre pairing H^1(O) x H^0(omega) -> H^1(omega), which is perfect. Consequently the (6,6)-specificity of the CE identification enters only through the separate requirement deg N = 2g-2-deg W_5+n = 0, i.e. through the Step-4 identification omega(Gamma) tensor N^{-1} = W_5, and not through the universal Pic^0 lemma at all. This localizes what FND-0074 blocks: the non-transport to neighbouring n is entirely a statement about the failure condition becoming a positive-degree Brill-Noether condition, while the determinantal scheme-structure machinery transports unchanged and can be reused verbatim for other (g,n) whenever the degree-zero condition is arranged.","numLines":79,"startLine":1,"totalLines":137,"truncatedByTokenCap":true}}}
