{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0138PgC7xWTe1QQLnP1Pk8Fn","type":"tool_result","content":"80	- `FND-0097` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'objects': ['balanced tetragonal CE bundle W', 'universal balanced tetragonal stack']}]: The hypothesis that the balanced CE bundle W SPLITS as W_4 + W_5 over the base is removable and should be replaced by the canonical filtration, which matters because the splitting can fail exactly where the campaign wants to use it. On the balanced locus F is fibrewise O(4)+O(5), so the relative Harder-Narasimhan filtration gives a canonical 0 -> L_5 -> F -> L_4 -> 0 over any base; dualizing and twisting yields a canonical 0 -> W_4 -> W -> W_5 -> 0 with W_4 the degree-20 sub and W_5 the degree-16 quotient. Since Gamma is finite over the base, both pi_* and restriction to Gamma stay exact on this sequence, and because coker(phi_4) = 0 the snake lemma gives coker(phi) isomorphic to coker(phi_5) as modules, hence Fit_0(coker phi) = Fit_0(coker phi_5) with no splitting used. By contrast a global splitting is a genuine extra hypothesis: the extension class lives in Ext^1_{P^1_B}(L_4, L_5), which sits in H^1(B, gamma'_*O(1)) (the fibrewise Ext vanishes, so no local obstruction is visible), and this need not vanish over a general base B, in particular over the universal balanced tetragonal stack that C66-GEO-Z hands to C66-GEO-H0 and C66-GEO-COMP. Downstream nodes should therefore state the CE reduction in filtered form; doing so both widens the theorem and removes an unverified hypothesis from any statement made over the universal balanced family.
81	- `FND-0098` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: For (g,n)=(6,6), any claim that the balanced CE failure model maps monomorphically into an evaluation-failure locus in M_{6,6} is equivalent to recovering the tetragonal pencil gamma from the degree-6 bundle L = W_5 ⊗ omega_C^{-1}, because M_{6,6} forgets gamma while a general genus-6 curve carries five distinct g^1_4's, so the underlying forgetful map is generically 5-to-1. Openness of the balanced splitting stratum inside the tetragonal locus is irrelevant to this and supplies no injectivity. The only standard recovery route is the identification L ≅ omega_C(-D) with D in the pencil (equivalently W_5 ≅ omega_C^2(-D)), which returns the pencil as |omega_C ⊗ L^{-1}|; an attempt that disclaims that identification has no remaining route to the monomorphism. Any mono claim additionally needs a well-defined source (the unordered, possibly non-reduced Div^6 model has no map to M_{6,6}), a well-defined target (CE failure is a condition on the pair (C,gamma), not on a point of M_{6,6}), and a stack-level full-faithfulness argument covering automorphism groups.
82	- `FND-0099` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: In the filtered CE reduction 0 -> W_4 -> W -> W_5 -> 0, exactness of pi_* is NOT supplied by finiteness of Gamma over the base. Finiteness of Gamma gives only exactness of restriction to Gamma (the sequence is locally split, so it survives ⊗ O_Gamma) and exactness of pushforward along Gamma -> B. Exactness of pi_* along the curve fibration, i.e. surjectivity of pi_*W -> pi_*W_5, requires R^1 pi_* W_4 = 0, which for (g,n)=(6,6) holds because deg W_4 = 4g+12-16 = 20 > 2g-2 = 10. Likewise coker(phi_4) = 0 requires H^1(W_4(-Gamma)) = 0, i.e. deg 14 > 10, plus commutation of the cokernel with base change and Nakayama to descend from geometric fibres to the sheaf. With those two vanishings the snake lemma and Fit_0(coker phi) = Fit_0(coker phi_5) are correct. Downstream filtered-CE arguments must cite the degree vanishings explicitly, and must recheck them for any (g,n) where deg W_4 <= 2g-2.
83	- `FND-0101` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: A weakest-sufficient lemma whose theorem_statement asserts a clause while the same artifact records a high-severity gap marker against that clause, and marks the corresponding claim with status 'gap', has not stated a weakest-sufficient theorem: a parenthetical such as '(residual base-relative writeup gap recorded)' is an admission, not a hypothesis, and does not conditionalize the assertion. Such clauses must be either conditionalized ('modulo X, ...'), demoted to a hand-off, or moved to the explicit exclusion list. The same discipline applies to internal conflicts between an asserted clause and the artifact's own exclusion list — as when a statement excludes non-closedness of Z^{bal} for want of a witness point while simultaneously asserting that a sub-locus 'is not a closed pure-codimension subvariety of M_{6,6}'.
84	- `FND-0102` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: For top-degree vanishing arguments that identify H^{4g-5}(Mod_g;V)≅(St⊗V)_{Mod} and kill odd Sp-inflated V by forcing S^-=0 on S=(St)_I via hyperelliptic/Birman–Hilden classes, it is not enough that a fixed hyperelliptic involution act as +id on C^{sym}: one must prove that the Mod-orbit of im(b: St(Σ_{0,2g+2})→St_g) generates St_g (equivalently, that a Broaddus cyclic generator lies in that orbit up to units). Arguments that treat maximal simplices or intersecting Humphries chains as Steinberg generators, or that invoke Mod-transitivity on chains to move arbitrary filling carriers into symmetric position, are invalid and do not establish S^-=0.
85	- `FND-0103` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: The h^0 range recorded for the C66-GEO-H0 stratification is not sharp, and one of its strata is empty. On every smooth genus-6 fibre of the balanced tetragonal CE family, M := omega_C^2 tensor W_5^vee is ALWAYS special, because h^1(M) = h^0(omega tensor M^vee) = h^0(L) = 1 + h^0(M) >= 1. Hence whenever h^0(M) > 0, Clifford's theorem applies and gives h^0(M) <= deg(M)/2 + 1 = 3, with equality only if C is hyperelliptic and M ~= (g^1_2)^{tensor 2} (the cases M ~= O_C and M ~= omega_C are excluded by deg M = 4 not in {0,10}). Therefore h^0(L) = 1 + h^0(M) is in {1,2,3,4} and NEVER 5, so the {h^0(L)=5} = {h^0(M)=4} stratum is empty, and h^0(L)=4 occurs only on hyperelliptic fibres. The C66-GEO-H0 stratification has at most four strata, and its top jump stratum is confined to the hyperelliptic locus.
86	- `FND-0104` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: Modulo GAP-Z-W5D (i.e. granting M ~= O_C(D) = gamma^*O_{P^1}(1)), the constancy question left open as GAP-H0-1 collapses to a single geometric exclusion. Indeed h^0(D) >= 2 always (gamma^* is injective on H^0(P^1,O(1))), and by FC-CLIFFORD-H0-BOUND h^0(D) <= 3 with equality only if C is hyperelliptic and D ~ 2 g^1_2. In that equality case |D| = |2H| = h^*|O_{P^1}(2)| for the hyperelliptic map h, so every pencil inside |D| is h^* of a pencil in |O_{P^1}(2)|, i.e. gamma = q o h with q: P^1 -> P^1 of degree 2 - gamma is non-primitive. Hence h^0(omega_C(-D)) = 1 + h^0(D) is in {3,4}, and 'h^0(omega_C(-D)) = 3 constantly on the whole balanced locus' is EQUIVALENT to 'no balanced fibre carries a tetragonal pencil factoring through a degree-2 map'. The remaining checkable question is exactly whether a non-primitive degree-4 pencil can have balanced CE splitting F = O(4)+O(5); this review does not settle that and does not assert the answer.
87	- `FND-0105` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: GAP-Z-W5D is not a deep gap; it localizes to exactly one normalization statement, and the packet already contains the arithmetic that pins the remaining freedom. The packet's own CE line-bundle convention is W_5 := (O_{P(E^vee)}(2) tensor gamma^*O_{P^1}(-5))|_C. Granting only the CE relative-canonical normalization in the weak form O_{P(E^vee)}(1)|_C ~= omega_{C/P^1} tensor gamma^*A = omega_C tensor gamma^*O(2) tensor gamma^*A for SOME line bundle A on P^1, one gets W_5 ~= omega_C^2 tensor gamma^*O(-1) tensor gamma^*A^2 = omega_C^2(-D) tensor gamma^*A^2. The residual twist is then forced away by degree: SRC-0004 Lemma 10.6 records deg(O_{P(E^vee)}(2)|_C) = 2(2g-2+4*2), i.e. deg(O_{P(E^vee)}(1)|_C) = 2g+6 = deg(omega_C tensor gamma^*O(2)), and a twist by gamma^*A shifts this by 4 deg A, so deg A = 0 and A ~= O_{P^1}. Hence W_5 ~= omega_C^2(-D), equivalently L ~= omega_C(-D) and M ~= O_C(D). Note the derivation needs balancedness only to make the labels f = (4,5) meaningful, not for the isomorphism itself. Consequence: the campaign should either add the CE relative-canonical normalization as a cited source line - one citation - or keep every downstream clause explicitly conditionalized on GAP-Z-W5D; what it should NOT do is what ATT-0057 does, namely relabel the gap as an established working-context fact.
