103	- `FND-0139` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: Under the campaign's standing fibrewise-balanced hypothesis F_b≅O(4)⊕O(5), the jump stratum is empty: B_4=∅, so h⁰(L)≡3 and B=B_3. Proof: ATT-0066/CLM-0066-3 (dual-confirmed by REV-0110 and REV-0116) shows B_4 is contained in the locus of hyperelliptic fibres on which γ_b factors as q∘h through the hyperelliptic double cover; FND-0125 shows that for a hyperelliptic genus-6 curve with a degree-four pencil the relations bundle is exactly F=O(2)⊕O(7). These are incompatible with balancedness on every geometric fibre, so no fibre lies in B_4. Consequences: GAP-H0-1 as carried by ATT-0066 and ATT-0089 is closed under the balanced hypothesis; the k=4 branch of any P^{k-1}-bundle or dim(Y)+k−1 statement is vacuous; and the pencil recovery of FC-COMP-PENCIL-RECOVERY-AUT holds on all of B rather than only on a stratum.
