109	- `FND-0148` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'characteristic': 0, 'objects': ['Z', 'U', 'S_6-ordering torsor', 'H_arith', 'H_geom'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-GEO-COMP', 'hypotheses': ['U connected qcqs over a field k', 'Z -> U a finite etale right S_6-torsor', 'U normal integral locally Noetherian for Irr(Z) = pi_0(Z)', 'U_{k-bar} connected for H_geom normal in H_arith and the geometric component count']}]: Let U be a connected quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme over a field k, u a geometric point, and Z -> U a finite etale right S_6-torsor. The group H in Irr(Z) = H\S_6 for the k-scheme Z is the image H_arith of pi_1^{et}(U,u) -> S_6. If U is normal, integral, and locally Noetherian, connected components of Z are its irreducible components, indexed by left H_arith-cosets; each has degree |H_arith| over U and stabilizer conjugate to H_arith. If, in addition, U_{k-bar} is connected, then H_geom := image(pi_1^{et}(U_{k-bar},u) -> S_6) is normal in H_arith, [S_6:H_arith] <= [S_6:H_geom], and after base change Z has [S_6:H_geom] geometric irreducible components of degree |H_geom|. Thus irreducibility over k is weaker than geometric irreducibility. This identifies the group but does not compute either monodromy image for the balanced tetragonal family.
