- `FND-0102` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: For top-degree vanishing arguments that identify H^{4g-5}(Mod_g;V)≅(St⊗V)_{Mod} and kill odd Sp-inflated V by forcing S^-=0 on S=(St)_I via hyperelliptic/Birman–Hilden classes, it is not enough that a fixed hyperelliptic involution act as +id on C^{sym}: one must prove that the Mod-orbit of im(b: St(Σ_{0,2g+2})→St_g) generates St_g (equivalently, that a Broaddus cyclic generator lies in that orbit up to units). Arguments that treat maximal simplices or intersecting Humphries chains as Steinberg generators, or that invoke Mod-transitivity on chains to move arbitrary filling carriers into symmetric position, are invalid and do not establish S^-=0.
