  "result_text": "I'll read all twelve JSON artifacts in full and extract the requested fields without adding extra mathematics.=== ATT-0065 (C66-GEO-Z) ===\n\ntheorem_statement (verbatim):\nLet k be a field of characteristic zero, B a locally Noetherian k-scheme, pi:C->B a smooth proper morphism with geometrically connected genus-g fibres, and x_1,...,x_n:B->C pairwise disjoint sections with n>=1 and Gamma=sum x_i(B). Let 0->W_4->W->W_5->0 be exact on C, with W_4,W_5 invertible, W locally free of rank two, and constant fibre degrees d_4,d_5 satisfying d_4-n>2g-2 and d_5-n=2g-2. Put phi:pi_*W->pi_*(W|Gamma), N=omega_{C/B} tensor W_5^vee(Gamma), P=Pic^0_{C/B}, a_N:B->P, and let e:B->P be the identity. Then Fit_0(coker phi)=a_N^*I_e; hence the intrinsic evaluation-failure scheme is exactly a_N^{-1}(e(B)), formation commutes with arbitrary locally Noetherian base change, the scheme represents relative triviality of N, and the identity descends along smooth atlases to locally Noetherian algebraic stacks. For the ambient comparison, additionally let s:P1_B->B, let p:X=P_{P1_B}(E^vee)->P1_B be a P2-bundle, let gamma:C->P1_B be a finite flat degree-four cover with CE embedding i:C->X, and assume its ideal has the standard degree-four CE resolution 0->O_X(-4) tensor p^*det(F)->O_X(-2) tensor p^*F->I_C->0 for a rank-two relations bundle F. Put q=s composed with p, script-W=O_X(2) tensor p^*F^vee, W=i^*script-W, and assume q_*script-W is finite locally free and commutes with arbitrary base change. If R^1s_*End(F)=0, then the restriction r:q_*script-W->pi_*W is surjective; consequently coker(phi composed with r)=coker(phi) canonically and compatibly with arbitrary base change, and the ambient and intrinsic zeroth Fitting ideals both equal a_N^*I_e. In particular, when (g,n)=(6,6) and every geometric fibre of F is O(4) direct-sum O(5), the canonical filtration induced by the O(5)-subbundle gives d_4=20,d_5=16, the intrinsic map has ranks 26->12, R^1s_*End(F)=0 automatically, and the actual ambient balanced CE evaluation-failure scheme is scheme-theoretically the locus where O_C(Gamma) is relatively isomorphic to W_5 tensor omega_{C/B}^{-1}.\n\nExplicit hypotheses / conditionals (quoted):\n- \"B a locally Noetherian k-scheme\"\n- \"d_4-n>2g-2 and d_5-n=2g-2\"\n- \"assume its ideal has the standard degree-four CE resolution ...\"\n- \"assume q_*script-W is finite locally free and commutes with arbitrary base change\"\n- \"If R^1s_*End(F)=0, then the restriction r:q_*script-W->pi_*W is surjective\"\n- \"when (g,n)=(6,6) and every geometric fibre of F is O(4) direct-sum O(5)\"\n\ntheorem_scope:\n- base: \"locally Noetherian over a characteristic-zero field; no reducedness or irreducibility assumption; arbitrary locally Noetherian base change\"\n- g: 6, n: 6\n- generality: \"the intrinsic Fitting/Picard identity holds for all g>=1,n>=1 satisfying the two degree inequalities; the ambient comparison holds only under the explicit obstruction vanishing R^1s_*End(F)=0 and the stated equation-bundle base-change hypothesis; fibrewise balanced F supplies the obstruction vanishing, including the target (6,6) case\"\n- packet_snapshot: \"proof/packets/generated/C66-001-v4-39e87ba7e3784b68.md\"\n- not_covered: \"ambient comparison for unbalanced relations bundles with R^1s_*End(F) nonzero; h0 strata; nonemptiness of the reduced-support open; images or closure in M_{6,6}; components, dimensions, stabilizers, lci/Gysin statements; Hodge, weight, purity, or Tate conclusions\"\n\nsummary:\nRepairs the ambient overstatement refuted by REV-0106 while retaining the independently confirmed intrinsic proof from ATT-0064. The universal nonreduced Picard calculation gives Fit_0(coker phi)=a_N^*I_e, and the filtered argument reduces evaluation to W_5 without a global splitting. For the actual ambient CE map, the standard degree-four CE resolution is tensored by script-W and pushed first along the P2-bundle. This gives the exact sequence 0->End(F)->p_*script-W->gamma_*W->0. Pushing along P1_B shows that the sole obstruction to surjectivity of q_*script-W->pi_*W is R^1s_*End(F). The theorem now assumes this vanishing exactly where it is needed. On the fibrewise O(4)+O(5) locus it follows from End(F_b)=O^2+O(1)+O(-1), so the balanced (6,6) ambient and intrinsic cokernels and Fitting schemes agree under arbitrary base change. No ambient assertion is made for the unbalanced counterexamples exposed by REV-0106.\n\nclaims:\n- CLM-0065-1 | status: proved | \"Under the two degree inequalities, pi_*W and pi_*(W|Gamma) are locally free of the asserted ranks with arbitrary base change, and Fit_0(coker phi)=I_{2n}(phi).\"\n- CLM-0065-2 | status: proved | \"For the universal Picard evaluation Phi, Fit_0(coker Phi)=I_e over arbitrary possibly nonreduced locally Noetherian bases.\"\n- CLM-0065-3 | status: proved | \"For a filtered rank-two W with d_4-n>2g-2, coker(phi) is canonically coker(phi_5), without assuming a global splitting.\"\n- CLM-0065-4 | status: proved | \"The intrinsic evaluation-failure ideal is a_N^*I_e, commutes with arbitrary locally Noetherian base change, represents relative triviality of N, and descends along smooth atlases.\"\n- CLM-0065-5 | status: proved | \"A fibrewise O(4)+O(5) relations bundle has a canonical O(5)-subbundle and O(4)-quotient, inducing the filtered W with degrees 20 and 16 at genus six.\"\n- CLM-0065-6 | status: proved | \"The standard degree-four CE resolution gives 0->End(F)->p_*script-W->gamma_*W->0, and the obstruction to q_*script-W->pi_*W being surjective maps through R^1s_*End(F).\"\n- CLM-0065-7 | status: proved | \"If R^1s_*End(F)=0, the ambient restriction is surjective and the ambient and intrinsic cokernel sheaves and Fitting ideals agree canonically and after arbitrary base change.\"\n- CLM-0065-8 | status: proved | \"Fibrewise balanced F implies R^1s_*End(F)=0 without a global splitting.\"\n- CLM-0065-9 | status: proved | \"At balanced (g,n)=(6,6), the actual ambient CE evaluation-failure scheme equals a_N^{-1}(e), equivalently the relative incidence O_C(Gamma)=W_5 tensor omega^{-1}, scheme-theoretically and after arbitrary base change.\"\n\ngap_markers: []\n\nmethods_used: proper-flat-perfect-complex-base-change; relative-picard-poincare-evaluation; fitting-ideal-base-change; relative-duality-trace; dual-numbers-serre-pairing; two-stage-nakayama-conormal-generation; filtered-snake-lemma-evaluation-reduction; smooth-atlas-descent; canonical-relative-hardernarasimhan-filtration; degree-four-ce-koszul-resolution; projective-bundle-derived-pushforward; relative-endomorphism-obstruction-vanishing\n\nfailed_approaches_addressed:\n- kind: review_repair | subject: \"REV-0106: equation-bundle base change was incorrectly treated as ambient restriction surjectivity\" | disposition: \"Repaired in Sections 8-9: the CE resolution exposes R^1s_*End(F) as the obstruction, the theorem assumes its vanishing, and balanced F proves it.\"\n- kind: review_repair | subject: \"wrong obstruction group H^1(X,O_X)\" | disposition: \"Removed entirely; the proof uses H^1(P1,End(F)) through the ideal-sheaf-twisted CE restriction sequence.\"\n- kind: working_context_constraint | subject: \"support-only scheme identification\" | disposition: \"Avoided: the intrinsic proof establishes equality of ideals, and the ambient proof establishes equality of cokernel sheaves before taking Fitting ideals.\"\n- kind: working_context_constraint | subject: \"global splitting inferred from fibrewise balancedness\" | disposition: \"Avoided: the canonical filtration and the R^1End(F) vanishing are both constructed fibrewise and descended by base change and Nakayama.\"\n- kind: working_context_constraint | subject: \"exactness of pi_* inferred from finiteness of Gamma\" | disposition: \"Avoided: Section 5 separately proves R^1pi_*W_4=0 and R^1pi_*W_4(-Gamma)=0.\"\n- kind: scope_constraint | subject: \"balanced incidence promoted to global geometry in M_{6,6}\" | disposition: \"Not claimed; image, closure, component, dimension, stabilizer, and Hodge/Tate questions remain downstream.\"\n\nproof_dependencies: [\"SRC-0004\"]\nexperiment_ids: []\nstatus: claimed_complete\nresult_type: lemma\n\n=== REV-0108 (of ATT-0065) ===\nverdict: \"confirmed\"\nNo fields named confirmed_claims / rejected_claims / scope_restrictions.\nchecked_claims (all verdict \"confirmed\"): CLM-0065-1, CLM-0065-2, CLM-0065-3, CLM-0065-4, CLM-0065-5, CLM-0065-6, CLM-0065-7, CLM-0065-8, CLM-0065-9, CHK-SCOPE (\"The theorem does not overclaim unbalanced ambient comparison, image/closure in M_{6,6}, components, dimensions, stabilizers, lci/Gysin, or Hodge/Tate conclusions.\")\nproof_dependency_checks: SRC-0004 confirmed.\n\nCaveats/limitations (quoted):\n- CHK-SCOPE note: \"theorem_scope.not_covered and Section 10 match the written claims; the lemma is judged on its exact statement, not the global RED-0001 campaign theorem.\"\n- finding FC-AMBIENT-EQN-BUNDLE-REMAINS-HYP: \"Even after fibrewise balanced specialization kills R^1s_*End(F), ambient Fitting comparison still requires the separate hypothesis that q_*script-W is finite locally free and commutes with arbitrary base change; balancedness alone does not discharge equation-bundle freeness.\"\n- strongest_attack tertiary: \"balanced specialization still carries the equation-bundle freeness/BC hypothesis on q_*script-W; the writeup correctly retains that hypothesis rather than claiming it follows from fibrewise O(4)+O(5).\"\n- strongest_attack secondary: \"R^1s_*End(F)=0 is only sufficient for surjectivity of r (the connecting map in (8.4) could vanish even if R^1 is nonzero). Outcome: does not break the theorem, which assumes the vanishing as a hypothesis and verifies it on the balanced locus.\"\n- CLM-0065-4 note: \"No coarse-space claim is made.\"\n\n=== REV-0109 (of ATT-0065) ===\nverdict: \"confirmed\"\nNo fields named confirmed_claims / rejected_claims / scope_restrictions.\nchecked_claims (all verdict \"confirmed\"): binding-check,