{-1} and M=omega_{C/B}^{\u22972}\u2297W_5^vee. Assume the standard weak CE normalization fibrewise: O_{P(E^vee)}(1)|_{C_b}\u2245omega_{C_b/P^1}\u2297gamma_b^*A_b for A_b\u2208Pic(P^1_{k(b)}). Then: (H1) on every geometric fibre, deg L=6, deg M=4, chi(L)=1, and h^0(L)=1+h^0(M); M is special and Clifford's theorem gives h^0(M)\u2a7d3. The normalization forces A_b\u2245O, hence W_{5,b}\u2245omega_{C_b}^{\u22972}(-D_b), L_b\u2245omega_{C_b}(-D_b), and M_b\u2245O_{C_b}(D_b)=gamma_b^*O(1), so h^0(L_b)\u2208{3,4}. (H2) On the underlying space of B, B_4={b:h^0(L_b)=4} is closed and B_3={b:h^0(L_b)=3} is its open complement. If B_k is given its reduced locally closed scheme structure, then pi_*L over B_k is locally free of rank k and commutes with base change. Moreover B_4 is contained in the locus of hyperelliptic fibres on which gamma_b is non-primitive, factoring through the hyperelliptic double cover. (H3) Let I=Hilb^6(C/B)\u00d7_{Pic^6(C/B)}B be the Abel\u2013Jacobi incidence over the section [L]. It is closed, represents relative effective divisors Gamma with O(Gamma) relatively isomorphic to L, and satisfies I\u00d7_B B_k\u2245P((pi_*L|_{B_k})^vee), a P^{k-1}-bundle. Thus the degree-six linear system is a P^2-bundle over B_3 and a P^3-bundle over B_4, but need not be a projective bundle over all of B and is not globally identified with Proj(pi_*L). (H4) Let I^dist be the distinct-support open and let tilde I=Conf_6(C/B)\u00d7_{Hilb^6(C/B)}I. Then tilde I->I^dist is a finite \u00e9tale S_6-torsor at stack level, with neither side reduced artificially. On Conf_6(C/B), the scheme-theoretic equality of ATT-0048, CLM-0048-4, CLM-0048-5 and CLM-0048-7, confirmed by REV-0091 and REV-0092, identifies tilde I exactly with the CE Fitting evaluation-failure locus Z_ev. No assertion is made that B_4 is empty, that I^dist is nonempty on every fibre, or that the full nonreduced Hilbert incidence outside the ordered distinct-support locus is covered by ATT-0048.\n\nExplicit hypotheses / conditionals (quoted):\n- \"Assume the standard weak CE normalization fibrewise: O_{P(E^vee)}(1)|_{C_b}\u2245omega_{C_b/P^1}\u2297gamma_b^*A_b for A_b\u2208Pic(P^1_{k(b)}).\"\n- \"If B_k is given its reduced locally closed scheme structure\"\n- \"No assertion is made that B_4 is empty, that I^dist is nonempty on every fibre, or that the full nonreduced Hilbert incidence outside the ordered distinct-support locus is covered by ATT-0048.\"\n\ntheorem_scope:\n- base: \"locally Noetherian over a characteristic-zero field\"\n- dependency_scope: \"ATT-0048 is used only on the ordered pairwise-distinct configuration stack, exactly within its six-disjoint-sections and smooth-atlas descent scope\"\n- exclusions: \"emptiness of B_4 (GAP-H0-1), reduced-support nonemptiness on every fibre, dimension or codimension in M_{6,6}, components, stabilizers, closure, smoothness, monomorphic embedding into M_{6,6}, and all Hodge/Tate conclusions\"\n- g: 6, n: 6\n- generality: \"fibrewise balanced tetragonal Casnati\u2013Ekedahl families with the canonical filtered quotient W_5 of ATT-0048 and the standard weak CE relative-canonical normalization\"\n\nsummary:\nProves the weakest scheme-correct h^0 stratification of the balanced tetragonal residual degree-six system. The only fibrewise values are 3 and 4; the corresponding Abel\u2013Jacobi linear systems are respectively P^2- and P^3-bundles, and the h^0=4 locus is confined to non-primitive hyperelliptic covers. Globally the system is the closed Abel\u2013Jacobi/Hilbert incidence rather than Proj(pi_*L). On the ordered distinct-support locus, and only there as required by the verified dependency's scope, it agrees scheme-theoretically with Z_ev by ATT-0048, REV-0091 and REV-0092. Emptiness of the jump stratum remains open.\n\nclaims:\n- CLM-0066-1 | status: proved | \"For L=W_5\u2297omega^{-1} and M=omega^{\u22972}\u2297W_5^vee on every balanced genus-6 geometric fibre, deg L=6, deg M=4, chi(L)=1, and h^0(L)=1+h^0(M); M is special and h^0(M)\u2a7d3.\"\n- CLM-0066-2 | status: proved | \"Under the weak CE normalization, M_b\u2245gamma_b^*O(1), so h^0(M_b)\u2208{2,3} and h^0(L_b)\u2208{3,4}.\"\n- CLM-0066-3 | status: proved | \"B_4={h^0(L)=4} is closed, B_3={h^0(L)=3} is open, and B_4 lies in the hyperelliptic non-primitive locus.\"\n- CLM-0066-4 | status: proved | \"On each reduced stratum B_k, pi_*L is locally free of rank k and base-change compatible, and the relative linear system is a P^{k-1}-bundle.\"\n- CLM-0066-5 | status: proved | \"Across the jump, the correct global degree-six linear system is the closed Abel\u2013Jacobi incidence I=Hilb^6(C/B)\u00d7_{Pic^6(C/B)}B, not an unqualified Proj(pi_*L).\"\n- CLM-0066-6 | status: proved | \"On the ordered distinct-support configuration stack, the pullback of I equals Z_ev scheme-theoretically and maps to the unordered distinct-support incidence as a finite \u00e9tale S_6-torsor.\"\n\ngap_markers: []  (argument_markdown names open gap GAP-H0-1: \"whether B_4 is empty for balanced covers\"; also \"nonemptiness of the distinct-support open on every fibre; all component, dimension, stabilizer, closure and codimension questions; and all Hodge/Tate consequences. In particular chi(L)=1 proves only that the full Abel\u2013Jacobi fibre is nonempty, not that it contains a reduced divisor.\")\n\nmethods_used: riemann-roch-and-serre-duality; clifford-theorem-for-special-degree-four-line-bundles; ce-relative-canonical-normalization; upper-semicontinuity-h0-stratification; grauert-cohomology-and-base-change; abel-jacobi-hilbert-incidence; verified-fitting-ideal-dependency; stack-level-ordered-distinct-support-torsor\n\nfailed_approaches_addressed: []\n\nproof_dependencies:\n- ATT-0048 (attempt): \"Verified C66-GEO-Z dependency; supplies CLM-0048-4, CLM-0048-5, CLM-0048-6 and CLM-0048-7.\"\n- REV-0091 (confirmation_review): \"First independent confirmation of CLM-0048-1 through CLM-0048-7.\"\n- REV-0092 (confirmation_review): \"Second independent confirmation of CLM-0048-1 through CLM-0048-7.\"\n- SRC-0004 (source): \"CE convention W_f=(O(2)\u2297gamma^*O(-f))|_C and degree formula deg W_f=4g+12-4f.\"\n- FND-0105 (adjudicated_finding): \"Weak CE relative-canonical normalization used fibrewise.\"\n\nexperiment_ids: []\nstatus: claimed_complete\nresult_type: lemma\n\n=== REV-0110 (of ATT-0066) ===\nverdict: \"confirmed\"\nNo fields named confirmed_claims / rejected_claims / scope_restrictions.\nchecked_claims (all verdict \"confirmed\"): CLM-0066-1 through CLM-0066-6; H1-RR-Clifford-normalization; H2-stratification-nonprimitive; H3-AJ-vs-Proj; H4-torsor-Zev.\nproof_dependency_checks (all confirmed): ATT-0048, REV-0091, REV-0092, SRC-0004, FND-0105, C66-GEO-Z.\n\nCaveats/limitations (quoted):\n- CLM-0066-2 note: \"Normalization is a hypothesis (FND-0105 discipline), not an internal CE derivation.\"\n- CLM-0066-3 note: \"Emptiness of B_4 correctly not claimed (GAP-H0-1).\"\n- H2 note: \"Theorem (H2) holds; one-way non-primitive containment only.\"\n- H3 note: \"Theorem (H3) holds; dual P^{k-1} models on B_3 and B_4 without global Proj claim.\"\n- H4 note: \"Theorem (H4) holds within dual-confirmed Conf_6 Fitting scope.\"\n- FND-0105 dep note: \"Weak CE relative-canonical normalization assumed fibrewise as theorem hypothesis; ... Not treated as unconditional CE theorem.\"\n- strongest_attack: \"Scope discipline (stack-level S_6-torsor, no one-sided reduction, explicit non-claims for B_4 emptiness, I^dist nonemptiness, and nonreduced Hilbert outside Conf_6) matches FND-0058/0083/0104 residual gaps without overclaim. ... the implication is correct; only the converse/emptiness under balancedness remains open as the attempt states.\"\n\n=== REV-0116 (of ATT-0066) ===\nverdict: \"confirmed\"\nNo fields named confirmed_claims / rejected_claims / scope_restrictions.\nchecked_claims (all verdict \"confirmed\"): CLM-0066-1 through CLM-0066-6.\nproof_dependency_checks (all confirmed): ATT-0048, REV-0091, REV-0092, SRC-0004, FND-0105.\n\nCaveats/limitations (quoted):\n- CLM-0066-4 note: \"The restriction to reduced strata is load-bearing and is correctly imposed: over a non-reduced base constancy of h^0 alone is insufficient\"\n- FC-H0-NONREDUCED-GRAUERT: \"fibrewise constancy of h^0(L_b) is NOT sufficient for pi_*L to be locally free or base-change compatible: Grauert genuinely requires a reduced base. ... even if GAP-H0-1 resolves with B_4 = empty so that h^0(L) = 3 identically, the relative linear system still need not be a P^2-bundle over a non-reduced base\"\n- FC-H0-NEGATIVE-CLAUSES-ARE-DISCLAIMERS: \"The negative clauses in C66-GEO-H0 clause (H3) \u2014 'need not be a projective bundle over all of B' and 'is not globally identified with Proj(pi_*L)' \u2014 are scope disclaimers, not proved existential statements, and must not be cited downstream as establishing that the degree-six system fails to be a projective bundle. No witness base with a nonempty jump stratum is exhibited ... and GAP-H0-1 leaves B_4 = empty open\"\n- strongest_attack: \"A third, weaker attack concerns H3's negative clauses ... read as existential assertions they would require a witness that the attempt does not supply, since GAP-H0-1 leaves B_4 possibly empty. ... residual risk is one of downstream citation. ... asserting the S_6-torsor at stack level only, where FND-0075 confirms it. ... no lemma-to-campaign overreach is present.\"\n- theorem_scope exclusions remaining: emptiness of B_4; reduced-support nonemptiness; dimension/codimension in M_{6,6}; components; stabilizers; closure; smoothness; monomorphic embedding into M_{6,6}.\n\n=== ATT-0088 (C66-COMP-RANK) ===\n\ntheorem_statement (verbatim):\nLet k be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, S a locally Noetherian k-scheme, pi:C->S smooth and proper with geometrically connected genus-six fibres, s:P->S a P1-bundle, gamma:C->P finite flat of degree four with Tschirnhausen bundle E (gamma_*O_C = O_P direct-sum E^vee, E of rank three), p:X=P_P(E^vee)->P the associated P2-bundle in the packet convention p_*O_X(1)=E, i:C->X the Casnati-Ekedahl embedding, and F a rank-two bundle on P. Assume: (CE) the ideal of i has the standard degree-four CE resolution 0->O_X(-4) tensor p^*det(F)->O_X(-2) tensor p^*F->I_C->0; (BAL) F restricted to every geometric fibre of s is O(4) direct-sum O(5); (N) on every geometric fibre, O_X(1)|_C is isomorphic to omega_{C/P1} tensor gamma^*A for some A in Pic(P1). Put W=i^*(O_X(2) tensor p^*F^vee) with the canonical filtration 0->W_4->W->W_5->0 induced by the O(5)-subbundle of F, L=W_5 tensor omega_{C/S}^{-1}, D=gamma^*O_P(1); O_P(1), hence W_4,W_5,L,D, is well defined only up to twist by a line bundle pulled back from S, and every assertion below is invariant under such a twist. THEN: (I) On every geometric fibre: (I.1) A is trivial, W_5=omega_C^{tensor 2}(-D), L=omega_C(-D), deg(L)=6, chi(L)=1, deg(W_4)=20, deg(W_5)=16; (I.2) C is not hyperelliptic; (I.3) h^0(O_C(D))=2, h^0(L)=3, h^1(L)=2, so |L| is a projective plane, and every summand of E has degree at least two; (I.4) the fixed part of |L| has degree at most one, hence is reduced, and the moving part is base-point-free with three sections; (I.5) the non-reduced locus Delta in |L| is closed of dimension exactly one, so the reduced-support locus |L|^red = |L| minus Delta is a nonempty dense open subset of dimension two and is not closed in |L|; (I.6) the ordered incidence {(p_1,...,p_6) in C^6 pairwise distinct with p_1+...+p_6 in |L|} is nonempty, smooth of pure dimension two, and a finite etale S_6-torsor of degree 720 over |L|^red. (II) Let B=Conf_6(C/S) be the complement of the big diagonal in the six-fold fibre product, with its six tautological pairwise-disjoint sections, universal divisor Gamma, evaluation phi:pi_*W->pi_*(W|Gamma), N=omega_{C/S} tensor W_5^vee(Gamma), a_N:B->Pic^0_{C_B/B} and identity section e. Then pi_*W and pi_*(W|Gamma) are locally free of ranks 26 and 12, every geometric fibre of phi has rank 11 or 12, and: (II.1) I_j(phi)=O_B for every j<=11, while I_12(phi)=Fit_0(coker phi)=a_N^*I_e cuts out the closed subscheme Z=a_N^{-1}(e(B)), whose formation commutes with arbitrary locally Noetherian base change; (II.2) the naive maximal-minor expectation for a 26-to-12 map is codimension 15 and the filtered 11-to-6 expectation is codimension 6, whereas the geometric fibres of Z->S have pure dimension two, i.e. codimension four in the fibres of B->S, the excess being 6-4=2=h^1(L). (III) Assume in addition S reduced. Then pi_*L is locally free of rank three, AJ=P_S(pi_*L) is a Zariski-locally trivial P2-bundle carrying a universal relative degree-six divisor, its etale locus U (the reduced-support open) is S-smooth of pure relative dimension two and surjective onto S, and the S_6-torsor of orderings of the universal divisor over U is canonically isomorphic to Z. Consequently: (III.1) Z->S is smooth and surjective of pure relative dimension two; if moreover S is of finite type over k, every irreducible component of Z and of U dominates an irreducible component of S and has dimension equal to the dimension of that component plus two; (III.2) the closed immersion Z->B is a regular immersion of pure codimension four, its conormal sheaf I_Z/I_Z^2 is locally free of rank four, and the conormal sequence 0->I_Z/I_Z^2->Omega_{B/S}|_Z->Omega_{Z/S}->0 is exact and locally split; (III.3) with delta:T_{B/S}=pi_*O_Gamma(Gamma)->R^1pi_*O_C the connecting map of 0->O_C->O_C(Gamma)->O_Gamma(Gamma)->0, the sequence 0->T_{Z/S}->T_{B/S}|_Z->(R^1pi_*O_C)|_Z->Exc->0 is exact on Z with Exc=coker(delta)|_Z canonically isomorphic to (R^1pi_*L) tensor M_univ, locally free of rank two, where M_univ is the tautological line bundle on Z determined by O(Gamma)=L tensor pi^*M_univ; dually 0->Exc^vee->(pi_*omega_{C/S})|_Z->I_Z/I_Z^2->0 is exact with Exc^vee = pi_*(omega_{C/S} tensor L^vee) tensor M_univ^{-1}, whose fibres are the two-dimensional spaces H^0(C,O_C(D)) of the tetragonal pencils. No assertion is made about images, closure, components, stabilizers, purity, codimension or Gysin maps in M_{6,6}, about unbalanced splitting types or h^0-jumping strata, about nonreduced bases in Part III, or about Hodge, weight or Tate type.\n\nExplicit hypotheses / conditionals (quoted):\n- \"(CE) the ideal of i has the standard degree-four CE resolution ...\"\n- \"(BAL) F restricted to every geometric fibre of s is O(4) direct-sum O(5)\"\n- \"(N) on every geometric fibre, O_X(1)|_C is isomorphic to omega_{C/P1} tensor gamma^*A for some A in Pic(P1)\"\n- \"(III) Assume in addition S reduced.\"\n- \"if moreover S is of finite type over k, every irreducible component of Z and of U dominates an irreducible component of S and has dimension equal to the dimension of that component plus two\"\n- \"No assertion is made about images, closure, components, stabilizers, purity, codimension or Gysin maps in M_{6,6}, ...\"\n\ntheorem_scope:\n- base: \"algebraically closed field of characteristic zero; S locally Noetherian for Parts I-II; Part III additionally assumes S reduced, and the component-dimension formula in (III.1) additionally assumes S of finite type over k. Statements over an algebraic stack hold on a smooth atlas and descend, since every construction used (Grauert local freeness on a reduced base, Sym^6 and Conf_6, projectivization, Fitting ideals, relative duality) is smooth-local on the base.\"\n- g: 6, n: 6\n- generality: \"Part II (rank strata and minor ideals) uses only (CE), (BAL) and the ATT-0065 hypotheses; Parts I and III use (N) in addition. Gamma is always the universal divisor of six pairwise-disjoint tautological sections, i.e. the base is the ordered configuration space, which is exactly where the ATT-0065 disjoint-section hypothesis holds; no statement is made for an arbitrary relative degree-six divisor. The Clifford and jet-incidence arguments of Part I are specific to (g,deg L)=(6,6); the determinantal and excess bookkeeping of Parts II-III is written so that only the stated degree inequalities are used.\"\n- hypotheses: \"(CE) standard degree-four Casnati-Ekedahl ideal resolution, exactly as in the ATT-0065 theorem hypotheses; (BAL) fibrewise F = O(4)+O(5); (N) fibrewise CE relative-canonical normalization O_X(1)|_C = omega_{C/P1} tensor gamma^*A. (N) is carried as an explicit hypothesis throughout and is never asserted; it is the packet's undischarged relative-canonical normalization, and every clause depending on it is stated under it rather than gap-marked.\"\n- not_covered: \"unbalanced CE splitting types; h^0-jumping strata; nonreduced bases in Part III (no local-freeness, projective-bundle, smoothness, regular-immersion or excess claim is made there); base-point-freeness of L on the balanced locus, which is neither asserted nor denied; images, closure, components, stabilizers, purity, codimension, lci status or Gysin/localization for the pair (M_{6,6},Z); the classifying map to M_{6,6} and its injectivity or stabilizers; any Hodge, weight, purity or Tate conclusion; characteristic p; integral coefficients and coarse-space statements.\"\n\nsummary:\nComputation-lane lemma for C66-COMP-RANK. Under (CE)+(BAL)+(N) it proves that on EVERY balanced geometric fibre h^0(L)=3 without jumping, that the fixed part of |L| has degree at most one, and that |L| contains a reduced divisor, so the reduced-support open is dense and the ordered Conf_6 incidence is nonempty, smooth of pure dimension two: this discharges the packet frontier obligation on fibrewise nonemptiness, and does so WITHOUT assuming L base-point-free, by killing the fixed part with Clifford and treating the moving part with a two-jet incidence count. The minor-ideal table of the CE evaluation is completed: I_j(phi)=O_B for all j<=11 and I_12(phi)=Fit_0(coker phi)=a_N^*I_e (the last imported from the twice-confirmed ATT-0065, whose six-disjoint-sections hypothesis is exactly met on the ordered configuration base). Over a reduced base the rank-drop scheme Z is identified with the S_6-torsor of orderings over the reduced-support open of the P2-bundle P_S(pi_*L), hence is smooth and surjective over S of relative dimension two, and is regularly embedded in Conf_6(C/S) with codimension four and locally free conormal of rank four; the excess is computed as coker of the Abel-Jacobi differential, canonically (R^1pi_*L) tensor M_univ with the tautological twist retained. The lci and excess conclusions are obtained from smoothness and an explicit conormal computation, not from the blocked expected-versus-actual codimension numerology.\n\nclaims:\n- CLM-0088-1 | status: proved | \"Under (CE), (BAL) and (N), on every geometric fibre the residual twist A is trivial, so W_4=omega_C^2, W_5=omega_C^2(-D), L=omega_C(-D), deg(W_4)=20, deg(W_5)=16, deg(L)=6 and chi(L)=1.\"\n- CLM-0088-2 | status: proved | \"Under (CE) and (BAL) alone, no balanced geometric fibre is hyperelliptic.\"\n- CLM-0088-3 | status: proved | \"Under (CE), (BAL) and (N), every balanced geometric fibre has h^0(O_C(D))=2, h^0(L)=3 and h^1(L)=2, so |L| is a projective plane and h^0(L) does not jump on the balanced locus; moreover every summand of E has degree at least two.\"\n- CLM-0088-4 | status: proved | \"On every balanced geometric fibre satisfying (N), the fixed part of |L| has degree at most one, hence is reduced, and the moving part is base-point-free of degree 5 or 6 with exactly three sections.\"\n- CLM-0088-5 | status: proved | \"On every balanced geometric fibre satisfying (N), |L| contains a divisor of six pairwise distinct points; the non-reduced locus is closed of dimension exactly one; the reduced-support open is nonempty, dense, of dimension two and not closed in |L|; and the ordered incidence in Conf_6(C) is nonempty, smooth of pure dimension two, and a finite etale S_6-torsor of degree 720 over the reduced-support open.\"\n- CLM-0088-6 | status: proved | \"Over B=Conf_6(C/S) with its six tautological disjoint sections, pi_*W and pi_*(W|Gamma) are locally free of ranks 26 and 12, every geometric fibre of phi has rank 11 or 12, I_j(phi)=O_B for every j<=11, and I_12(phi)=Fit_0(coker phi)=a_N^*I_e with formation commuting with arbitrary locally Noetherian base change.\"\n- CLM-0088-7 | status: proved | \"The corank-one locus of the 26-to-12 evaluation has naive determinantal expectation 15 and filtered 11-to-6 expectation 6, while its actual fibres over the balanced locus have pure dimension 2, i.e. codimension 4 in the fibres of Conf_6(C/S)->S; the excess relative to the filtered expectation is 6-4=2=h^1(L).\"\n- CLM-0088-8 | status: proved | \"Over a reduced locally Noetherian base, pi_*L is locally free of rank three, AJ=P_S(pi_*L) is a Zariski-locally trivial P2-bundle whose etale locus U is S-smooth of relative dimension two and surjective onto S, and Z is canonically isomorphic to the S_6-torsor of orderings of the universal divisor over U; hence Z->S is smooth surjective of pure relative dimension two, and over a finite-type base every component of Z and of U dominates a component of S with dimension equal to that of the dominated component plus two.\"\n- CLM-0088-9 | status: proved | \"Over a reduced base, the closed immersion Z->Conf_6(C/S) is a regular immersion of pure codimension four, its conormal sheaf is locally free of rank four, and the conormal sequence is exact and locally split.\"\n- CLM-0088-10 | status: proved | \"Over a reduced base there is a canonical exact sequence 0->T_{Z/S}->T_{B/S}|_Z->(R^1pi_*O_C)|_Z->Exc->0 on Z with Exc=coker of the relative Abel-Jacobi differential canonically isomorphic to (R^1pi_*L) tensor M_univ, locally free of rank two; dually 0->Exc^vee->(pi_*omega_{C/S})|_Z->I_Z/I_Z^2->0 with Exc^vee=pi_*(omega_{C/S} tensor L^vee) tensor M_univ^{-1}, whose fibres are the two-dimensional spaces of the tetragonal pencils.\"\n\ngap_markers: []\n\nmethods_used: clifford-theorem-with-equality-cases; fixed-part-moving-part-decomposition; two-jet-incidence-dimension-count; casnati-ekedahl-quadric-sequence-from-ideal-resolution; projective-bundle-derived-pushforward; hyperelliptic-pushforward-splitting; filtered-snake-lemma-evaluation-reduction; fitting-minor-ideal-rank-stratification; relative-picard-poincare-evaluation; grauert-local-freeness-reduced-base; abel-jacobi-projective-bundle-model; s6-torsor-of-orderings-of-the-universal-divisor; regular-immersion-of-smooth-base-schemes; relative-abel-jacobi-differential-excess-sequence; relative-duality-conormal-identification; smooth-atlas-descent\n\nfailed_approaches_addressed: []\n\nproof_dependencies: [\"ATT-0065\", \"SRC-0004\"]\nexperiment_ids: []\nstatus: claimed_complete\nresult_type: lemma\n\n=== REV-0139 (of ATT-0088) ===\nverdict: \"confirmed\"\nNo fields named confirmed_claims / rejected_claims / scope_restrictions.\nchecked_claims (all verdict \"confirmed\"): CLM-0088-1 through CLM-0088-10.\nproof_dependency_checks (all confirmed): ATT-0065, SRC-0004.\n\nCaveats/limitations (quoted):\n- CLM-0088-7 note: \"The codimension expectations and excess are bookkeeping only: 15 for the unfiltered maximal-minor presentation, 6 for the filtered presentation, and 6-4=2=h^1(L). No Gysin or cohomological conclusion is inferred.\"\n- CLM-0088-10 note: \"Stack/coarse-moduli, rational/integral, cohomology/Borel-Moore, Kunneth, spectral-sequence, automorphism, semisimplification, motivic, algebraicity/tautological-generation and stable-pair issues are not used by this exact lemma.\"\n- strongest_attack: \"The strongest attack is the compressed fixed-part-degree-one branch of the discriminant argument: without separately tracking the fixed point, the two-jet incidence could fail to prove that the non-reduced locus has dimension exactly one. The argument survives because in that branch the discriminant is the union of the moving-system discriminant and the hyperplane of divisors containing the fixed point; both have dimension at most one, while the everywhere-nonempty two-jet incidence forces a one-dimensional image. This also preserves the finite etale degree-720 ordered cover over the complementary reduced-support open.\"\n\n=== REV-0142 (of ATT-0088) ===\nverdict: \"confirmed\"\nNo fields named confirmed_claims / rejected_claims / scope_restrictions.\nchecked_claims (all verdict \"confirmed\"): CLM-0088-1 through CLM-0088-10; two-jet-dimension-split; grauert-reduced-base; src-0004-sign-convention.\nscope_checks (list, not named scope_restrictions):\n- \"stack versus coarse space: the S_6-torsor and the regular immersion are stated on Conf_6 and on the stack of pairwise-disjoint sections, not on coarse M_{6,6}\"\n- \"rational versus integral coefficients: unused; no cohomology of local systems is claimed\"\n- \"cohomology degree versus Borel-Moore homology degree: unused; the lemma makes no Hodge or weight claim\"\n- \"Poincare duality and Tate twists: expressly excluded\"\n- \"Gysin and Kunneth shifts: expressly excluded for the pair (M_{6,6},Z)\"\n- \"degeneration or spectral-sequence differentials: unused\"\n- \"invariants versus coinvariants under graph automorphisms: unused\"\n- \"semisimplification versus actual Hodge-structure isomorphism: unused\"\n- \"predicted motives used as unconditional theorems: unused\"\n- \"pure Tate silently upgraded to algebraic or tautological generation: unused\"\n- \"omitted stable pairs: unbalanced CE types, h^0-jumping strata, and nonreduced bases in Part III are listed as not covered\"\n\nCaveats/limitations (quoted):\n- CLM-0088-4 note: \"No claim is made that L itself is base-point-free.\"\n- CLM-0088-5 note: \"The construction lives in Conf_6(C), not on coarse M_{6,6}.\"\n- CLM-0088-7 note: \"The artifact draws no regularity, depth, lci, Gysin, or Tate conclusion from the excess identity.\"\n- grauert-reduced-base: \"Part III assumes S reduced exactly so that constant fibre dimensions h^0(L)=3 and h^1(L)=2 yield local freeness and base change. No local-freeness, projective-bundle, smoothness, regular-immersion, or excess claim is made over a nonreduced base.\"\n- strongest_attack: \"No stack-versus-coarse, rational-versus-integral, Poincare-twist, Gysin, spectral-sequence, invariants-versus-coinvariants, semisimplification, predicted-motive, or omitted-stable-pair error is load-bearing: the theorem is a scheme-level lemma over Conf_6 and expressly excludes M_{6,6} images, Hodge/Tate type, unbalanced strata, and nonreduced bases in Part III.\"\n\n=== ATT-0086 (C66-COMP-COMP) ===\n\ntheorem_statement (verbatim):\nLet B be a reduced locally Noetherian scheme over a characteristic-zero field carrying a smooth genus-six degree-four Casnati\u2013Ekedahl family whose relations bundle is fibrewise balanced, F_b \u2245 O(4) \u2295 O(5), and which satisfies the weak CE relative-canonical normalization used in ATT-0066. For the canonical quotient W_5 put L=W_5\u2297\u03c9^{-1}. Then h^0(C_b,L_b)=3 for every geometric b in B; equivalently, the jump stratum B_4={b:h^0(L_b)=4} is empty. Consequently the closed degree-six Abel\u2013Jacobi incidence Hilb^6(C/B)\u00d7_{Pic^6(C/B)}B is a Zariski-locally trivial P^2-bundle over B. Thus a proposed balanced component decomposition containing a nonempty B_4/P^3 piece is false.\n\nExplicit hypotheses / conditionals (quoted):\n- \"Let B be a reduced locally Noetherian scheme\"\n- \"which satisfies the weak CE relative-canonical normalization used in ATT-0066\"\n- theorem_scope.normalization_role: \"The normalization is needed to obtain h^0(L_b)\u2208{3,4}; emptiness of the h^0=4 stratum itself follows from Clifford equality and incompatibility of hyperelliptic degree-four covers with balanced CE relations.\"\n\ntheorem_scope:\n- base: \"reduced locally Noetherian schemes over a characteristic-zero field\"\n- exclusions: \"No assertion is made for nonreduced bases, about nonemptiness of the reduced-support or ordered Conf_6 incidence, about components or dimensions of the image in M_{6,6}, stabilizers, closure, lci/Gysin structure, Hodge purity, Tate support, Tate assembly, or RED-0001.\"\n- g: 6, n: 6\n- generality: \"smooth finite-flat degree-four tetragonal CE families with fibrewise relations splitting F_b=O(4)\u2295O(5), the canonical filtered quotient W_5, and the weak relative-canonical normalization of FND-0105\"\n- normalization_role: as quoted above.\n\nsummary:\nThe dual-confirmed ATT-0066 stratification has no P^3 jump piece on the balanced locus. A point of B_4 would force a hyperelliptic genus-six curve, but every degree-four map from such a curve factors through its hyperelliptic map and has unbalanced CE relations. Under the stated normalization only h^0=3 remains, so the full Abel\u2013Jacobi incidence is a P^2-bundle on a reduced base. This is an analytic proof; no finite experiment is used.\n\nclaims:\n- CLM-0086-1 | status: proved | \"For a balanced genus-six degree-four CE fibre, the locus h^0(L)=4 is empty; this exclusion does not require the weak relative-canonical normalization.\"\n- CLM-0086-2 | status: proved | \"Under the weak CE normalization, h^0(L)=3 fibrewise; over a reduced locally Noetherian base the full Abel\u2013Jacobi incidence is a Zariski-locally trivial P^2-bundle, with no B_4/P^3 piece.\"\n\ngap_markers: []  (argument_markdown remaining-gaps paragraph: \"The weak relative-canonical normalization remains an explicit hypothesis. The proof does not establish nonemptiness of the reduced-support open, ordered Conf_6 incidence or full S_6 monodromy. It also gives no image dimension, closure, lci/Gysin class, Hodge purity, Tate support, or Tate assembly in M_{6,6}. In particular it does not prove that W_{\u221216}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6}) is a direct sum of Q(8), so RED-0001 remains unresolved.\")\n\nmethods_used: verified-dependency-h0-stratification; riemann-roch-and-serre-duality; clifford-equality-case; castelnuovo-severi-factorization; casnati-ekedahl-relation-bundle-section-count; grauert-cohomology-and-base-change-on-reduced-base; abel-jacobi-hilbert-incidence\n\nfailed_approaches_ad