EV-0116, FND-0125, FND-0105, SRC-0004, FND-0103, FND-0107.\n\nCaveats/limitations (quoted):\n- CLM-0086-2 note: \"The reducedness restriction honors the nonreduced-base obstruction, and the statement stays over schemes rather than silently widening to a stack base ... purity, Tate support, Tate assembly and RED-0001 are explicitly excluded\"\n- FND-0105 dep: \"the weak CE relative-canonical normalization is carried as an explicit hypothesis ... It enters only to pin h^0(L) \u2208 {3,4}; emptiness of the h^0=4 stratum is independent of it.\"\n- FND-0107 dep: \"The artifact does not confuse the closed incidence with the reduced-support open, nor call that open closed.\"\n- finding balanced-normalized-fibres-have-reduced-general-divisor caveat: \"Not proved or asserted by the reviewed artifact ... It says nothing about relative (as opposed to fibrewise) density over a general base, nothing about S_6 monodromy, and nothing about Tate type.\"\n- strongest_attack residual: \"The correct residual reading is scope, not error: this lemma advances the geometry/computation node only, discharges no Tate obligation, and its novelty is modest, since FND-0104 and FND-0125 already compose to B_4 = \u2205; what is new is the normalization-free route to hyperellipticity and the model-free splitting count.\"\n- RUNNER-UP on CLM-0086-1 parenthetical: \"a normalization leak inside the claim that no normalization is needed. ... The claim nonetheless survives ... Since the theorem_statement carries the normalization as a hypothesis anyway, this touches only an auxiliary parenthetical, not the theorem.\"\n\n=== REV-0138 (of ATT-0086) ===\nverdict: \"confirmed\"\nNo fields named confirmed_claims / rejected_claims / scope_restrictions.\nchecked_claims (all verdict \"confirmed\"): CLM-0086-1, CLM-0086-2.\nproof_dependency_checks (all confirmed): ATT-0066, REV-0110, REV-0116, FND-0125, FND-0105, SRC-0004, FND-0103, FND-0107.\n\nCaveats/limitations (quoted):\n- CLM-0086-2 note: \"No stack widen