12	      "claim_id": "CLM-0086-2",
13	      "note": "Under the stated normalization M \u2245 \u03b3^*O(1) = O(D), so h^0(M) \u2265 2 (\u03b3^* is injective on H^0(P^1,O(1))) and h^0(M) \u2264 3 by Clifford, i.e. h^0(L) \u2208 {3,4}; CLM-0086-1 removes 4, leaving h^0(L)=3 on every geometric fibre \u2014 consistent with the internal cross-check that |L| is then a g^2_6 whose residual \u03c9\u2297L^{-1} is exactly the degree-4 pencil. The second half is correctly hypothesis-guarded: B reduced with h^0 constant = 3 are precisely Grauert's hypotheses, so p_*L is locally free of rank 3 with base change, and the Abel\u2013Jacobi model Hilb^6 \u00d7_{Pic^6} B \u2245 P((p_*L)^\u2228) is Zariski-locally trivial because the projectivization of a locally free rank-3 sheaf is. The reducedness restriction honors the nonreduced-base obstruction, and the statement stays over schemes rather than silently widening to a stack base, so neither a constant-rank lifting argument nor a smooth-atlas descent line is owed. No coarse-versus-stack, integral-coefficient, cohomological-versus-BM-degree, Tate-twist, Gysin/K\u00fcnneth, differential, invariants-versus-coinvariants, or semisimplification step occurs anywhere in this lemma; purity, Tate support, Tate assembly and RED-0001 are explicitly excluded and resolves_exact_target=false is recorded.",
