30	      "statement": "The exclusion of balanced CE relations on a genus-six hyperelliptic degree-four cover needs neither an explicit curve model nor the CE relative-canonical normalization. For \u03b3 = q\u2218h, E = O(1)\u2295O(4)^2 is forced for EVERY degree-2 map q, because deg q_*O(-7) = -8 by Euler characteristic and h^0(q_*O(-7)\u2297O(3)) = h^0(O(-1)) = 0 pushes the larger summand to degree \u2264 -4. Given only that, h^0(Sym^2E(-6)) = 9, while h^0(C, O_{P(E^\u2228)}(2)|_C \u2297 \u03b3^*O(-6)) = 7 follows from degree alone (deg = 36 - 24 = 12 > 2g-2 = 10, so h^1 = 0 and Riemann\u2013Roch gives 7), with no identification of the line bundle and hence no use of O_{P(E^\u2228)}(1)|_C \u2245 \u03c9_{C/P^1}. Left-exactness then gives h^0(F(-6)) \u2265 2, excluding splitting types (4,5) and (3,6) among a+b=9.",
